<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Foreningsbanken '96 profit up.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Foreningsbanken '96 profit up.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Foreningsbanken was expected to post a 1996 profit of 1.13 billion crowns after loan losses, a Reuter poll showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 1.06 and 1.25 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The bank posted an operating profit of 811 million crowns in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>In 1995 the bank posted a pre-tax operating profit of 745 million crowns.</p>
<p>Loan losses are expected to run at 990 million crowns, the poll showed.</p>
<p>Forecasts for a dividend ranged from 0.50 crown to 0.90 crown.</p>
<p>For 1997 and 1998 the bank expected to post a profit after loan losses of 1.3 billion crowns in both years.</p>
<p>The bank is due to publish its 1996 result on February 18.</p>
<p>Sources who participated in this survey included Enskilda, Handelsbanken, Penser, Swedbank, Carnegie, JP Morgan, Kleinwort Benson and Nordbanken.</p>
